![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The `buildSummary` function currently performs six separate `.filter()` traversals over the `rows` array. Since this registry manages a 3530-question universe, executing multiple full-array iterations is inefficient and creates unnecessary intermediate arrays. Consolidating these checks into a single `for...of` loop reduces the complexity to a single pass (O(N)), improving both performance and memory usage. Additionally, ensure that we defensively handle the case where `rows` is null or undefined, returning a consistent empty summary structure.

```javascript
function buildSummary(rows) {
  const safeRows = rows || [];
  const summary = {
    questionCount: safeRows.length,
    textOnlyRows: 0,
    visualRequiredRows: 0,
    lowConfidenceRows: 0,
    unavailableEvidenceRows: 0,
    blockedEvidenceRows: 0,
    attemptableInBetaRows: 0,
  };

  for (const row of safeRows) {
    if (row.posture?.requiresImageContext === true) {
      summary.visualRequiredRows++;
    } else {
      summary.textOnlyRows++;
    }
    if (includesLowConfidence(row)) {
      summary.lowConfidenceRows++;
    }
    if (row.posture?.evidenceAvailabilityStatus === 'unavailable') {
      summary.unavailableEvidenceRows++;
    }
    if (isBlockedEvidence(row)) {
      summary.blockedEvidenceRows++;
    }
    if (row.posture?.attemptableInBeta === true) {
      summary.attemptableInBetaRows++;
    }
  }

  return summary;
}
```

